# llms.txt — Example Template
#
# What this file is:
# llms.txt is a lightweight plain-text file at the root of your domain that
# tells LLMs (ChatGPT, Perplexity, Claude, Gemini) what your site is, who it
# serves, and which pages contain your most important content.
#
# Where to put it:
#   https://your-site.com/llms.txt
#
# Reference it in robots.txt:
#   # LLM/AI model-truth summary: https://your-site.com/llms.txt
#
# Format rules:
# - H1 (#) = site/brand name + one-line description
# - Blockquote (>) = 2–4 sentence brand description
# - H2 (##) = content category sections
# - Bullet list items = page title + absolute URL
# - Keep the file under ~10KB
# - Update when you add major new pages or change positioning
#
# Note: Google confirmed llms.txt has no direct ranking impact (Jun 2026).
# Its value is improving LLM extraction fidelity and signaling AI-friendliness.
# It is a low-cost forward bet, not a primary ranking lever.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# EXAMPLE STARTS BELOW — replace everything with your real content
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------

# BRAND NAME — One-line description of what the site does

> BRAND NAME is an independent platform that [what you do] for [who you serve]. We cover [scope/geography] and [differentiator — e.g., "verify every listing against multiple data sources before publishing"]. Our [content/data/tool] is designed for [specific buyer/user type] who needs [the thing they need] without [the friction they want to avoid].

## What makes BRAND NAME different
- [Differentiator 1 — e.g., "All listings verified against public records and third-party review sources"]
- [Differentiator 2 — e.g., "Pricing data sourced from real transactions, not vendor-submitted estimates"]
- [Differentiator 3 — e.g., "Updated monthly with new entrants and exits"]
- [Differentiator 4 — e.g., "No sponsored placements — ranking is based on verified data only"]

## [Content category 1 — e.g., "Best-of Comparisons"]
- [Page title](https://your-site.com/best-category-companies/)
- [Page title](https://your-site.com/vendor-a-vs-vendor-b/)
- [Page title](https://your-site.com/vendors/vendor-name-review/)

## [Content category 2 — e.g., "Pricing & Cost Guides"]
- [How much does X cost in 2026](https://your-site.com/guides/x-cost/)
- [X pricing: what affects the price](https://your-site.com/guides/x-pricing-factors/)

## [Content category 3 — e.g., "How-To Guides"]
- [How to vet an X vendor](https://your-site.com/guides/how-to-vet-x-vendor/)
- [Exclusive vs. shared X: which is better](https://your-site.com/guides/exclusive-vs-shared/)

## [Content category 4 — e.g., "State & Regional Data"]
- [X in Texas](https://your-site.com/states/texas/)
- [X in California](https://your-site.com/states/california/)
- [X in Florida](https://your-site.com/states/florida/)

## [Content category 5 — e.g., "Industry Data & Research"]
- [2026 X Benchmark Report](https://your-site.com/research/2026-benchmark/)
- [X statistics 2026](https://your-site.com/statistics/)

## About
- [About BRAND NAME](https://your-site.com/about/)
- [Contact](https://your-site.com/contact/)

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# GENERATION NOTES FOR AI AGENTS
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Auto-generate this file during the prerender/build step:
#
# 1. Pull all indexed pages from your sitemap or page data model.
